ready: 1
kind: rule
id: health.rule.anxiety
display_id: RULE-HEALTH-ANXIETY
module: health
title: How anxious the agent's memory is
summary: Anxiety is a weighted average of six dimensions, each scored from 0 to 100, over the dimensions
  that can be measured at that moment.
inputs:
- name: context figures
  source: The caller or hook
  source_kind: parameter
- name: checkpoint age
  source: The latest checkpoint
  source_kind: stored
- name: review backlog
  source: Pending suggestions
  source_kind: stored
- name: identity confidence
  source: Identity synthesis
  source_kind: return
- name: uncertain count
  source: Active memories' confidence after decay
  source_kind: derived
- name: epoch age
  source: The current epoch
  source_kind: stored
table:
  columns:
  - dimension
  - weight
  - scores 0 when
  - scores 100 when
  - resolved by
  rows:
  - - context pressure
    - '0.25'
    - under half the context limit is used
    - the context is full
    - checkpoint, then let the runtime compact
  - - unsaved work
    - '0.20'
    - a checkpoint is under 15 minutes old
    - no checkpoint for 3 hours or more
    - checkpoint
  - - review backlog
    - '0.15'
    - no suggestion or held deletion waits
    - 20 or more wait or one is older than 14 days
    - suggestions review
  - - identity coherence
    - '0.15'
    - identity confidence is 0.9 or more
    - identity confidence is 0.3 or less
    - consolidate, then save a self-narrative
  - - memory uncertainty
    - '0.15'
    - no active memory is uncertain
    - a fifth or more of active memories are uncertain
    - verify or revise beliefs; give feedback
  - - epoch staleness
    - '0.10'
    - the current epoch is under 6 months old
    - the current epoch is 2 years old or there is none
    - close the epoch and start a new one
calculations:
- name: dimension score
  expr: linear between its 0 and 100 points, clamped to 0..100
- name: score
  expr: Σ(weight × dimension score) ÷ Σ(weight) over measurable dimensions, rounded
- name: level
  expr: the anxiety level whose range holds the score
- name: recommended actions
  expr: each dimension scoring 50 or more, highest weighted score first, with the call that resolves it
default: A dimension that cannot be measured, such as context pressure without context figures, is left
  out of both sums
constants:
- health.const.anxiety-levels
- health.const.uncertain-below
rationale: 'Leaving unmeasured dimensions out of the average, rather than counting them as calm, is what
  lets one calculation serve every caller: the command line knows nothing about context, while a hook
  near compaction does. Processing debt is not a dimension, because sleep handles it without the agent;
  counting it would push agents to spend their work on upkeep.'
